Preserve Fil-C pointer provenance and capabilities across OPcache persistence and arena load

Fix three classes of Fil-C pointer-provenance bugs in PHP 7.4 ext/opcache:

1. ARENA_REALLOC() in zend_accelerator_util_funcs.c added the delta
   (ZCG(arena_mem) - current_persistent_script->arena_mem) to ptr, keeping
   the SHM capability of ptr instead of rebasing onto ZCG(arena_mem).
2. The __AVX__/__SSE2__ 64-byte alignment blocks in ZendAccelerator.c,
   zend_persist.c, zend_persist_calc.c, zend_accelerator_util_funcs.c, and
   zend_file_cache.c cast pointers through (zend_uintptr_t ... & ~63L),
   stripping Fil-C capabilities, and used inline assembly / vector
   loads/stores in fast_memcpy() that strip pointer metadata when copying
   arena structs. Disable the AVX/SSE2 fast path under __FILC__ so the
   portable memcpy() and capability-preserving allocation paths are used.
3. Rebase opline->op{1,2}.zv onto (char*)op_array->literals in
   zend_persist.c (ZEND_USE_ABS_CONST_ADDR path) so pointers never retain
   the freed orig_literals capability.

--- a/ext/opcache/ZendAccelerator.c
+++ b/ext/opcache/ZendAccelerator.c
@@ -1376,7 +1376,7 @@
 	memory_used = zend_accel_script_persist_calc(new_persistent_script, NULL, 0, 0);
 
 	/* Allocate memory block */
-#if defined(__AVX__) || defined(__SSE2__)
+#if (defined(__AVX__) || defined(__SSE2__)) && !defined(__FILC__)
 	/* Align to 64-byte boundary */
 	ZCG(mem) = zend_arena_alloc(&CG(arena), memory_used + 64);
 	ZCG(mem) = (void*)(((zend_uintptr_t)ZCG(mem) + 63L) & ~63L);
@@ -1496,7 +1496,7 @@
 	memory_used = zend_accel_script_persist_calc(new_persistent_script, key, key_length, 1);
 
 	/* Allocate shared memory */
-#if defined(__AVX__) || defined(__SSE2__)
+#if (defined(__AVX__) || defined(__SSE2__)) && !defined(__FILC__)
 	/* Align to 64-byte boundary */
 	ZCG(mem) = zend_shared_alloc(memory_used + 64);
 	if (ZCG(mem)) {
@@ -4145,7 +4145,7 @@
 	memory_used = zend_accel_script_persist_calc(new_persistent_script, NULL, 0, 1);
 
 	/* Allocate shared memory */
-#if defined(__AVX__) || defined(__SSE2__)
+#if (defined(__AVX__) || defined(__SSE2__)) && !defined(__FILC__)
 	/* Align to 64-byte boundary */
 	ZCG(mem) = zend_shared_alloc(memory_used + 64);
 	if (ZCG(mem)) {
